;; FH-ERROR-002 — reset, and the once-per-generation safe intent.
;;
;; A changed :reset-key clears the captured failure and re-mounts the child.
;; Under repeated failures WITHIN one generation the safe `:on-error` intent
;; (and the private egress record) fire EXACTLY ONCE — not "at least once" —
;; and a fresh failure generation, after a reset and another throw, reports
;; again.
{:fh/id "FH-ERROR-002"
 :fh/law
 "A changed :reset-key by rf= clears the captured failure and re-mounts the child; under repeated failures within one generation the safe intent and the private egress fire exactly once, and a new failure generation after a reset reports exactly once again."

 :on-error   [:telemetry/ui-render-failed]
 :view-id    :app.workspace/workspace-page
 :phase      :render
 :frame-id   :rf/default

 ;; The two caller-owned reset values that bracket the two generations.
 :reset-key-1 :revision-1
 :reset-key-2 :revision-2

 ;; Drive this many failed captures + promotions within EACH generation.
 :repeated-failures 5

 ;; The exact-count assertion: one intent (and one egress record) PER
 ;; generation, no matter how many repeated failures, and exactly two across
 ;; the two generations bracketing one reset.
 :intents-per-generation        1
 :egress-records-per-generation 1
 :total-intents-after-one-reset 2
 :total-egress-after-one-reset  2

 ;; The state-machine facts a reset and a re-capture leave.
 :after-first-capture {:status :failed :generation 1}
 :after-reset         {:status :clear  :did-reset? true}
 :after-same-key      {:did-reset? false}
 :after-recapture     {:status :failed :generation 2}}
